<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">EXECUTIVE PITCH TO THE EVALUATION JURY (30 SECONDS)</div>
  <p><em>"Respected Judges, in operational marine navigation, <strong>a hallucinated heading, risk score, or boundary clearance can cost human lives and coastal vessels</strong>. Therefore, our architectural foundation is built on <strong>Hierarchical Agentic Orchestration with Deterministic Guardrails</strong>. We strictly decouple probabilistic language interpretation from deterministic navigational physics:</em></p>
  <p><em>1. <strong>Probabilistic Layer (NLU & Explanation Agents):</strong> Performs natural language understanding across English, Hindi, and Marathi, and articulates transparent briefings.</em><br/>
  <em>2. <strong>Deterministic Layer (Marine, GIS, Weather, and Risk Engines):</strong> Executes 100% auditable mathematical computations—including Haversine geodesy, ray-casting geofencing, A* risk-penalized pathfinding, and 5-factor deterministic risk matrices.</em></p>
  <p><em><strong>The LLM is never allowed to calculate coordinates, distances, or safety scores; it only explains the mathematical proofs generated by our specialist engines.</strong>"</em></p>
</div>

<h2>1. End-to-End 7-Stage Multi-Agent Workflow</h2>
<p>The ORCA multi-agent engine follows a strict, 7-stage directed execution pipeline that guarantees response integrity, offline resilience, and mathematical explainability:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 12%;">Stage</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Agent / Engine</th>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Type</th>
      <th style="width: 43%;">Core Responsibility</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 1</strong></td>
      <td><strong>NLU Agent</strong><br/>(<code>nlu_agent.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-blue">Hybrid</span><br/>Regex + Gazetteer + LLM</td>
      <td>Extracts intents, entities (harbor, target species, time window), and user language (EN/HI/MR).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 2</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Master Orchestrator</strong><br/>(<code>orchestrator.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-green">Deterministic</span><br/>State Machine</td>
      <td>Cross-turn session memory, clarification short-circuits, and parallel dispatch to specialists.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 3</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Marine & PFZ Agent</strong><br/>(<code>marine_agent.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-green">Deterministic</span><br/>Spatial SQL + API</td>
      <td>Retrieves Potential Fishing Zones (PFZs), SST thermal breaks, and Chlorophyll-a fronts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 4</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Weather & Hazard Agent</strong><br/>(<code>weather_hazard_agent.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-green">Deterministic</span><br/>Ocean State Client</td>
      <td>Evaluates significant wave height (Hs), swell, wind velocity, rain, and IMD/INCOIS alerts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 5</strong></td>
      <td><strong>GIS & Geospatial Agent</strong><br/>(<code>gis_agent.py</code> & <code>navigator.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-green">Deterministic</span><br/>Geodesic & Pathfinding</td>
      <td>Calculates Haversine distances, initial bearings, A* nautical routes, and IMBL geofencing.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 6</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Deterministic Risk Engine</strong><br/>(<code>risk_engine.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-green">Deterministic</span><br/>Mathematical Matrix</td>
      <td>Computes 5-component weighted risk (0–100) and enforces non-negotiable safety overrides.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Stage 7</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Decision & Explanation Agent</strong><br/>(<code>decision_agent.py</code>)</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-blue">Semantic</span><br/>Structured GenAI</td>
      <td>Synthesizes numerical proofs into actionable advice in English, Hindi, or Marathi.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

