<h2>3. Python Imports Breakdown & Technical Justifications</h2>

<p>Every single Python import across our agent architecture was intentionally chosen for memory efficiency, execution speed, and zero runtime failures:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Import / Library</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Agent Location</th>
      <th style="width: 55%;">Technical Reason & Architectural Justification</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>import math</code></td>
      <td><code>gis_agent.py</code>, <code>navigator.py</code></td>
      <td>Provides high-performance C-optimized trigonometric routines (<code>sin</code>, <code>cos</code>, <code>atan2</code>, <code>radians</code>) required for microsecond geodesic distance and bearing calculations.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from pydantic import BaseModel, Field</code></td>
      <td>All schemas (<code>nlu.py</code>, <code>risk.py</code>, <code>marine.py</code>)</td>
      <td>Pydantic V2 provides compiled Rust-speed schema validation. Enforces strict type contracts between agents and prevents malformed data payloads.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from datetime import datetime, timedelta</code></td>
      <td><code>nlu_agent.py</code>, <code>fishing_reasoning_engine.py</code></td>
      <td>Calculates temporal horizons, converts dynamic colloquial strings (<em>"tomorrow morning"</em>, <em>"next 3 days"</em>) to ISO UTC stamps, and computes tidal windows.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>import re</code></td>
      <td><code>nlu_agent.py</code></td>
      <td>Enables fast deterministic regular expression tokenization for harbor names, ports, and multi-lingual Indian script pattern extraction without network calls.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from shapely.geometry import Point, Polygon, shape</code></td>
      <td><code>gis_agent.py</code></td>
      <td>Industry-standard GEOS computational geometry library for testing spatial intersections against complex 100+ vertex maritime border polygons.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from google import genai</code></td>
      <td><code>llm_client.py</code></td>
      <td>Official Google GenAI SDK for interacting directly with Gemini 2.5/3.1 Flash-Lite models with support for structured JSON schema outputs.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>import tenacity</code></td>
      <td><code>llm_client.py</code></td>
      <td>Implements deterministic exponential backoff and retry policies for external network API calls, preventing unhandled connection drops at sea.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from fastapi import FastAPI, Query</code></td>
      <td><code>app/main.py</code></td>
      <td>High-throughput asynchronous ASGI web server framework with automatic OpenAPI documentation and native JSON serialization.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from supabase import create_client, Client</code></td>
      <td><code>supabase_client.py</code></td>
      <td>Connects to cloud PostgreSQL database hosting operational marine tables, user authentication, and chat history vectors.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>from pathlib import Path</code></td>
      <td><code>navigator.py</code></td>
      <td>Provides operating-system agnostic path resolution for GeoJSON maritime boundary datasets on Windows, Linux, and macOS servers.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

